Z||000008||Archie||04-26-2001||12:56 AM||||NIFE and the participants in the Paxton, IL show on May 5, 2001, are planning to add another event to the published schedule for that show.<P>Those who attend the Fiero Fest 2001 at Bob Steiger's on the 5th, will be able to participate in a parade of Fieros that will join The Hot Rod Power Tour for about 10 miles. <P>We are finishing up a pass out sheet that we will hand out to those at the show. This sheet will detail the plan we've put together to greet the Power Tour as it makes it's way to the Paxton fuel stop. We have worked out a plan that shouldn't interfere with the other things going on at Bobs. We figure to be away froms Bob's 30 or 40 minutes but, I'm sure you will come back with lots to talk about for the rest of the day.<P>As soon as the pass out sheet is finished I will post it here for you to read.<P>This is just one more reason to attend the event at Bob's.<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000009||Archie||04-26-2001||12:18 PM||||This is the letter that will be passed out to the attendees at Bob's show on 5-5-01.<P>Saturday, May 5, 2001<P>Dateline Paxton, IL<P>As you know, you are here to participate in Bob Steigers' annual FIERO FEST 2001.<P>There is also another event today that we are also going to try to participate in <P>As it turns out, today we have a unique opportunity to receive some national press for our marque and our Club. Many of you are aware of a publication called Hot Rod Magazine. Each year Hot Rod Magazine sponsors a cross-country cruse for car buffs called the Hot Rod Power Tour. This year the Power Tour starts in Pontiac, MI (to honor the 75th anniversary of the birth of Pontiac) and ends in California.  Well, as it turns out, on May 5th at 11:30 the Power Tour has a fuel stop on I-57 at the Paxton exit  (mile marker 261). We have decided to have a group of Fieros greet the Power Tour as they pass near to us in Paxton. Arrangements have been made to have the group of Fieros from our event meet up with the Power Tour as they approach Paxton. In the current issue and in past issues, Hot Rod Magazine has invited all Clubs to join in the tour as it passes across the country. We have informed Hot Rod Magazine of our intentions, and our hope is that they will take some pictures and publish them in a future issue of the magazine. The publishers of Hot Rod also own several other magazines including Kit Car Magazine. Representatives of these magazines will also be on the tour.<P>The Power Tour will be spending the night of the 4th in Joliet, IL & will leave there to travel down I-57 to their scheduled overnight stay in Effingham. They will be leaving Joliet at 10:00 AM. In the latest issue of Hot Rod Magazine there is an article about a Yellow Fiero Formula owned by Phil Randolph. Phil has participated in the last 2 Power Tours and will be running in this event again this year. Our plan is to organize a group of Fieros that will meet up with the Power Tour. Phil has agreed to call us via cell phone when the tour is about 40 minutes from us.  The Fiero owners that want to participate will drive up RT45 to Buckley then proceed to join up with the tour as they pass down I-57. WE plan to enter I-57 going South and park on the right shoulder of I-57, and as the tour approaches, we will join in the group, as space is available. We will drive the 9 miles to the fuel stop at the Paxton Exit. From there our participants can mingle with the tour participants &/or head back to Twin Lakes Fiero. You just need to go East from the fuel stop to RT45 and turn left (North) to get back to Bob's for lunch!!<P>Archie||||reg||1
Z||000010||BBBAD GT||04-26-2001||01:20 PM||||Sounds cool....count me in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/V8Fiero/V8sig.jpg">        <P><A HREF="http://home.att.net/~nomercy5.0/V8Specs.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD V8 For Sale</A><P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||14
Z||000011||SloPonti||04-27-2001||12:01 AM||||count me in also! what time should we be at bob's so that we can take part in all of this?<BR>thanks<BR>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000012||Archie||04-27-2001||08:53 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by SloPonti:<BR><B>count me in also! what time should we be at bob's so that we can take part in all of this?<BR>thanks<BR>Rob</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The official start of Bob's event is 10 am, the Power Tour is scheduled to arrive in Paxton starting at 11:30.<P>My calculations indicate that our group of Fieros will be leaving Bob's at around 10:45. Phil (who will be travelling with the Tour) will call me on my Cell phone when he is 50 miles from Paxton. We will calculate the exact departure time from Bob's once we get that call.<P>Archie<p>[This message has been edited by Archie (edited 04-27-2001).]||||reg||1
